check=first-pass-converges
operator=dropped-effect
target=src/Amoebius/Host/Ensure.hs
mutation=replace | src/Amoebius/Host/Ensure.hs | observed <- reresolve (hostSubstrate current) | let observed = current
statement=Drop the re-resolve between steps, so every step after the first reads the config
statement=snapshot the run began with. A tool a step laid down is absent from that snapshot, so the
statement=driver walks the whole plan and still reports the requested tool missing. The argv it
statement=issues is unchanged -- every step still runs -- so the transcript's mutation rows stay
statement=authored and only the convergence verdict moves, which is what separates this from a
statement=driver that never probed at all.
